INT. CHEESEWORKS HEADQUARTERS - ELEVATOR - DAY

A glass elevator lined with laminated posters of cheddar wheels. A speaker plays soft jazz. Six employees stand shoulder to shoulder, each holding a coffee cup.

An INTERN, 20s, with a lanyard that reads GUEST, holds a clipboard. NADEZHDA FAIRBANKS, 40s, VP of Curds, adjusts her blazer. BARTHOLOMEW "BART" OKONKWO-REYES, 50s, Director of Rind, stares at the ceiling. Beside them, WINNIE TRAN, 30s, and PERCIVAL STONE, 30s, the Brie Brothers, share a single earbud. The sixth, MR. HOLLOWELL, 60s, the CEO, holds a golden wedge of cheese like a clutch purse.

The doors close. The elevator does not move.

NADEZHDA
Floor six, please.

BART ^
Floor six, please.

NADEZHDA
(to the intern)
Press six.

INTERN
I did.

WINNIE
It's stuck.

PERCIVAL
It's thinking.

MR. HOLLOWELL
Everyone stay calm. The cheese is not in danger.

The lights flicker. Nobody breathes. The intern takes a half step back and presses herself against a poster of gouda. The jazz cuts out.

MR. HOLLOWELL
Who are you, young lady?

INTERN
My name is Francesca. I've been an intern for three days.

MR. HOLLOWELL
Francesca. Do you know how to fix an elevator?

FRANCESCA
No, sir. I know how to fill out a form.

MR. HOLLOWELL
Then fill it out.

She opens the clipboard. Winnie and Percival hold up the earbud between them, and a tiny song leaks out.
